# Every real route is prerendered to its own HTML file at build time
# (see ssgOptions.includedRoutes in vite.config.js), so Netlify serves
# /work, /services, /privacy and the rest straight from disk. Netlify does
# not apply a redirect rule that would shadow an existing file unless the
# rule is forced with a "!", so this catch-all only ever fires for a path
# that genuinely has no page behind it.
#
# It used to read "/*  /index.html  200", which handed every unknown URL a
# byte-identical copy of the homepage with an HTTP 200 and the homepage's own
# canonical tag. Google reads that as a soft 404 across an unbounded set of
# paths. Now an unknown URL gets the real 404 page with a real 404 status.
